##RenderMan RIB-Structure 1.0
# Multi-threaded tile-fetch stress scene, spec 019 (019-tilesource-extraction)
# T012. A large, frontal, periodically-wrapped polygon textured with
# concurrency_rgb.tex (9-level mip pyramid, 16x16=256 tiles at the base
# level -- see fixtures/FIXTURES.md), diced at a fine ShadingRate so many
# micropolygon grids -- processed across many REYES buckets, hence many
# threads -- fault in many distinct tiles concurrently. The polygon spans
# well past the frame and wraps periodically, so multiple buckets/threads
# race to fault in the SAME early tile too (spec.md User Story 2
# acceptance scenario b), not just distinct ones (scenario a).
version 3.03
Hider "reyes"
Display "concurrency-scene.tif" "file" "rgba"
Projection "orthographic"
ShadingRate 0.25
Translate 0 0 4
Surface "paintedplastic" "texturename" ["concurrency_rgb.tex"]
WorldBegin
  LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [1]
  Patch "bilinear" "P" [-4 -4 0  4 -4 0  -4 4 0  4 4 0]
        "st" [0 0  8 0  0 8  8 8]
WorldEnd
